Apple today seeded the second betas of upcoming iOS 27.3 and iPadOS 27.3 updates to developers, with the software coming two weeks after <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/apple-seeds-first-ios-27-3-beta/">the first betas were released</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iOS-27.3-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071817" /><br/>
Registered developers can download the betas by going to Settings > General > Software Update and opting in to the developer beta.<br/>
<br/>
iOS 27.3 adds a new Vertical Tabs layout option that moves Safari tabs to the left side of the display. There's also an Adaptive <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-dark-mode/">Dark Mode</a> for Safari that can turn light sites darker when &zwnj;Dark Mode&zwnj; is activated.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI can do more in and across apps with support for actions in Calendar, Files, Journal, Mail, Maps, Messages, Music, Notes, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a>, Preview, Reminders, Safari, Shortcuts, and Weather.<br/>
<br/>
The new Health app is back, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> now supports Reachability, and there's a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> Selfie Sing feature if you want to capture videos of yourself while you do karaoke. There are more features too, with a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-3-beta-features/">list available in our iOS 27.3 beta guide</a>.<br/>
<br/>
